  "body": "## Result\n\nAdds an exact three-source common-core fan-in with simultaneous rank-one deviations. The source maps are \\(B_j=B+D_j\\), with a rank-48 shared core and three distinct rank-one \\(D_j\\) on 49 coordinates, so each direct \\(B_j\\) map has rank 49.\n\nFor arbitrary dirty sources, target, and scratch \\(t=d\\), the construction subtracts \\(Bd\\), gathers \\(S=x_1+x_2+x_3\\) into \\(t\\), adds \\(B(d+S)\\), restores \\(t\\), and applies all three deviations. The arbitrary dirty term cancels exactly. No clean row or source mutation is assumed.\n\n## Complete local cost screen\n\nThe baseline uses three rank-49 calls and three rank-one dispatch units. The construction uses two rank-48 core calls, three rank-one deviation calls, six rank-one gather/restore calls, and 11 dispatch units. At the selected exponent \\(a=836330098538459/500000000000000000\\), with \\(q=1-a\\), the difference is\n\n\\[\n3\\cdot49^q-2\\cdot48^q-17>28.\n\\]\n\nThis leaves at most 28 rank-one-equivalent units for additional parent/interface/program costs. The construction requires one 49-coordinate dirty row and up to two guard bits for an integer-valued lift; those charges must fit that budget and the supplier's row stock. The package does not claim that a live supplier seam has been found, does not change the selected profile, and claims no new \\(\\kappa\\).\n\n## Verification\n\nFrom the repository root:\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -O -B research/common-core-fanin-seed93550f9f/verify.py\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/common-core-fanin-seed93550f9f --check-only\n```\n\nThe direct verifier passes on Python 3.14.7. It checks ranks 48/1/49, all 245 binary basis columns of the arbitrary-dirty five-row interface, an integer-valued fixture, and four negative controls. The package metadata and source pins pass. Python 3.12 is not installed locally, so the registered Python 3.12 replay remains for CI.\n\n## Pins and overlap\n\nThe task card and SOURCES.json pin base `0b1cccf86e2f5132ed286a26ef0a681a495740ea`, selected-record SHA-256 `10b9e340fd8e354a37a0c4813c90e5de1dd42044b5f6aca4a3fc5a42b685fa32`, maintainer review, integration receipt, selected source manifest, and assembly certificate.\n\nNearest work is PR #1531's arbitrary-map DUO, PR #1518's atomic TRIO, PR #1524/Discussion #1579's equal-map common-B connector, and PR #1739's sequential rank-one source update. This construction treats three simultaneous distinct maps with rank-one deviations from a shared core. The final global Discussion refresh stalled in GitHub's GraphQL client; current PR pagination and REST checks of Discussions #1163, #1504, and #1579 found no exact overlap.\n\nPrepared with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance. No predecessor code was imported; no independent human review is claimed.\n",
